    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33452" root="فرد" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفْرَدٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرْدٌ</span>, second quarter. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence, as a
conventional term, <i>A single, simple, word</i> or
<i>vocable;</i>] <i>an expression of which a portion does
not denote a portion of its meaning:</i> (KT:) [pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفْرَدَاتٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <i>Singular,</i> as distinguished from
dual and plural. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفْرَادَاتُ الطِّبِّ</span> <i>The
simples of medicine; medicinal simples.</i>] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  And
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفْرَدٌ</span> signifies also <i>A wild bull.</i> (L. [See, again,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرْدٌ</span>, near the end.])

